WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.400
Hello.

2
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:11.360
I'm a professor of psychiatry at Seoul
National University Bundang Hospital.

3
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:17.540
In this eighth session, we will introduce
psychotherapy, a treatment other than medicine,

4
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:23.160
and mindfulness, and then practise
mindfulness together for a short time.

5
00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.410
You can talk with your doctor during visits,

6
00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:31.640
but regular counselling over a longer
time can also help your treatment.

7
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:37.400
There are several kinds of psychotherapy,
such as psychoanalytic supportive therapy,

8
00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:43.010
cognitive behavioural therapy, and
relationship-focused psychotherapy.

9
00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:48.710
It is best to start after the acute symptoms
have passed and you are fairly stable.

10
00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:52.030
If you are interested, talk with your doctor.

11
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.040
Mindfulness is the practice of focusing on
this present moment and accepting it as it is,

12
00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:00.690
without judging.

13
00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:04.570
It can help ease everyday
stress, anxiety and depression,

14
00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:09.010
and it is also one part of
dialectical behaviour therapy.

15
00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.620
First, choose one thing to focus on.

16
00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.660
Anything is fine, but something
concrete is better at the start.

17
00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:23.834
Your breathing, listening to music, the feeling
of your feet on the floor, a sunrise or sunset,

18
00:01:23.854 --> 00:01:30.840
a good book, playing with a pet, or walking:
choose something you can easily focus on.

19
00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:35.850
Then bring your attention to
that object and begin to focus.

20
00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:42.450
Once you have chosen what to look at, observe
it closely from every side with curiosity,

21
00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:45.950
as if you were seeing it for the first time.

22
00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:51.600
As you focus, your attention will
wander and many thoughts will come up.

23
00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:54.400
This is completely natural.

24
00:01:54.620 --> 00:02:00.520
The point is not to avoid getting distracted,
but to notice that you have been distracted.

25
00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.980
It does not matter whether you notice
right away or a few minutes later.

26
00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:09.530
Once you notice, gently guide your
attention back to the object.

27
00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:13.140
There is no need to blame yourself for losing focus.

28
00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.760
It is fine if your attention
wanders fifty times in one minute.

29
00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:23.000
Noticing, and gently coming back,
again and again, is mindfulness.

30
00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:27.670
There are two kinds of mindfulness practice.

31
00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:32.590
Informal practice is done during daily life,
such as washing dishes, brushing your teeth,

32
00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.230
or driving.

33
00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:40.890
Formal practice is done by setting aside
time to sit or lie down in a quiet place,

34
00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:46.150
such as thought-watching practice
or progressive muscle relaxation.

35
00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:48.430
Both are important.

36
00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:53.660
Now, let's practise briefly, using
your breathing as the object.

37
00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:56.480
Please sit in a comfortable position.

38
00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.970
Simply feel the breath coming in and going out.

39
00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:12.910
When a thought comes up, just notice, here is a thought.

40
00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.810
Then gently come back to your breathing.

41
00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:32.190
Well done.

42
00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:35.790
Noticing and coming back like this is mindfulness.

43
00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.800
There is no good or bad at mindfulness.

44
00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:45.080
Try practising steadily, even a few minutes a day.

45
00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:45.920
Next time,

46
00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:53.380
we will talk about lifestyle habits and the circadian
rhythm that help you overcome mood disorders.

47
00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.300
Thank you.
